0.3376.543Brull's baseline level indicates a fixed level or value, not a waveform. In this way, Brull teaches against the claimed invention that is based on the realization that a dominant part of the signal is periodic noise varying significantly over time, but having a periodic character exploited by the invention. (See, e.g., current application, page 7.)

