2.1533.84Kurtz teaches averaging the sum of amplitude and noise of "multiple time-based data series". This implies that a period of time over, e.g., five responses must elapse before an amplitude value is obtained. Kurtz therefore also teaches calculating a fixed level or value not reflecting the dynamic variation of noise.

